# The three grammar rules for question 1 are the ones marked below. The rest
# of this file exists only so that the specification is complete enough for
# PLCC to build it. Nothing about this language means anything, and the
# semantic section is deliberately empty: no methods, so nothing runs -- but
# PLCC still generates the classes, which is what you are here to look at.
skip  WS          '\s+'
token THIS        'this'
token IS          'is'
token EACH        'each'
token HAS         'has'
token MULTIPLE    'multiple'
token OCCURRENCES 'occurrences'
token ME          'me'
token AM          'am'
token TAKING      'taking'
token AND         'and'
token VAR         '\$\w+'
token OF          'of'
token CSIT        'CS\d+'
token DOT         '\.'
%
<Start:One>    ::= <Blah>
<Start:Two>    ::= <Many>
<Start:Three>  ::= <Classes>

<Blah:Goo>     ::= THIS <VAR> IS <Silly>                                   # (a)
<Many>         **= EACH <Rule> HAS MULTIPLE OCCURRENCES <OF> <Stuff>       # (b)
<Classes>      ::= ME AM TAKING <CSIT:c1> <CSIT:c2> AND <CSIT:c3>          # (c)

<Silly>        ::= DOT
<Rule>         ::= DOT
<Stuff>        ::= DOT
%
Python
